cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TSI-Denoising in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "TSI-Denoising: High-frequency surface-wave mode separation and three-station interferometry denoising for dense 1-D arrays"
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21853472"
authors:
  - family-names: Yuan
    given-names: Yusong
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-1138-7593"
    affiliation: "China University of Geosciences (Wuhan); University of Science and Technology of China"
  - family-names: Qiu
    given-names: Hongrui
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4219-0039"
    affiliation: "China University of Geosciences (Wuhan)"
abstract: >-
  TSI-Denoising is a Python package for processing ambient-noise
  cross-correlation waveforms recorded by dense one-dimensional arrays. It
  supports validated SAC ingestion, shared preprocessing, MASW dispersion
  analysis, four-component Rayleigh-wave mode separation, and iterative
  three-station interferometry denoising, with teaching workflows for the MARS
  DAS and Ramona Reservation array examples.
keywords:
  - surface waves
  - ambient noise
  - seismology
  - dense arrays
  - three-station interferometry
  - mode separation
  - MASW
  - distributed acoustic sensing
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/YuanYusung/TSI-Denoising"
